# Copy to .env.local (and set the same variables on the hosting platform).

# Public address of the live site (no trailing slash). Share previews on Facebook/WhatsApp,
# Google's canonical links and the sitemap all use it — set it to the real domain.
# (On Vercel the production domain is used automatically if this is left unset.)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://example.com

# Google Search Console: paste the code from the "HTML tag" verification method.
# GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# ── "Propose a project" form ──
# Proposals are emailed through this SMTP account. For Gmail:
#   1. Turn on 2-Step Verification for the Google account.
#   2. Create an App password: https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
#   3. Put the account address in SMTP_USER and the 16-character app password in SMTP_PASS.
# Without SMTP_USER / SMTP_PASS the form still works: it opens the visitor's email app
# with the proposal filled in, addressed to the team.
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
# Optional (defaults shown)
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=465
# Where proposals go (defaults to the contact email in src/data/team.ts)
# PROPOSALS_TO=baseera.ag@gmail.com
